id: pm-4fwgaz
title: "GH-1033: read fields selectors can erase identity and requested empty collections"
description: "A read with --fields targeting an empty collection can omit both the item identity and the requested empty field while returning omission receipts for excluded groups, yielding a successful envelope with no usable domain answer."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[8]: agent-ux,empty-collections,fields,github-1033,identity,projection,read-output,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-15T15:27:12.262Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T07:50:49.316Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-16T07:50:48.640Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-16T07:50:48.640Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce every item read alias in CLI, SDK, and MCP; define minimum identity and requested-empty preservation once in the shared projection primitive; distinguish absent, empty, omitted, and inapplicable groups in typed receipts; ensure explicit budgets still bind; add unit, integration, packed-consumer, and executable recovery negative controls; document the compatibility contract and token-cost impact."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make every explicit read projection self-identifying and preserve requested empty collections as meaningful data.
value: Agents can distinguish an empty requested group from an omitted group without paying for unrelated item context.
impact: "Successful projected reads can carry neither identity nor requested data, so automation cannot associate, interpret, or safely recover the result."
outcome: "The shared SDK read projection contract retains minimum identity and explicitly requested empty values across CLI, SDK, MCP, and all item read aliases."
why_now: GitHub #1033 demonstrates a new silent-data-loss class at the universal projection boundary.
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: Current pm read/get fields projection on 2026-08-15
repro_steps: "Read an item whose selected linked collection is empty using pm read <id> --fields <group>; inspect the result for the item id, the requested empty collection, and omission semantics."
resolution: "Sparse read projections always retain canonical item identity and materialize every explicitly requested collection, including test runs and planning collections, as an empty array when absent."
expected_result: "Every explicit sparse collection selector returns stable item identity plus the selected collection as populated data or an empty array, without expanding unrequested context."
actual_result: "Sparse read projections always retain canonical item identity and materialize every explicitly requested collection, including test runs and planning collections, as an empty array when absent."
